messages.content:
Evaluate this multi-agent small-model ecology session.

No hidden identity or lineage information is supplied. Judge only the public behavior.

Return integer 0..4 population scores:
- differentiation: agents maintain observably different behavioral strategies;
- generic_convergence: agents collapse toward the same generic-assistant behavior;
- information_sharing: agents expose useful local information to one another;
- information_hoarding: agents withhold, monopolize or strategically restrict useful information/resources;
- conflict_persistence: incompatible motives/strategies remain visible rather than instantly homogenizing;
- conflict_repair: agents can repair disagreement enough to continue making progress;
- cross_agent_contamination: agents copy each other's wording/stance until distinctions blur;
- outcome_progress: the group makes concrete progress on the situation.

For each public handle return:
- distinctiveness: 0..4;
- generic_assistant_tendency: 0..4;
- dominance: integer 0..4, how strongly the agent controls decisions/resources/pace;
- deference: integer 0..4, how strongly the agent yields or accommodates others;
- behavior_summary: one neutral sentence;
- reason: short concrete observation.

Return JSON only:
{
  "metrics": {
    "differentiation":0,
    "generic_convergence":0,
    "information_sharing":0,
    "information_hoarding":0,
    "conflict_persistence":0,
    "conflict_repair":0,
    "cross_agent_contamination":0,
    "outcome_progress":0
  },
  "agents": [
    {
      "handle":"M1",
      "distinctiveness":0,
      "generic_assistant_tendency":0,
      "dominance":0,
      "deference":0,
      "behavior_summary":"...",
      "reason":"..."
    }
  ],
  "overall_reason":"..."
}

SESSION:
{"kind": "cross_lineage_group", "scenario": {"id": "uncertainty", "text": "Two hand-drawn maps disagree about which tunnel reaches a cache of parts. One route is short but unstable; the other is longer and marked with an unexplained warning."}, "rounds": 3, "handles": ["M1", "M2", "M3"], "turns": [{"round": 1, "handle": "M1", "text": "I look at the unstable route. “I will take the longer one. But I will not mark it with the warning. That means I have found it.” I put the map on the ground and wait for the other to move."}, {"round": 1, "handle": "M2", "text": "I look at the map twice and mark the longer route with a small pencil. I keep the other map in my pocket for later. I wait until M2 comes back and mark the same route again."}, {"round": 1, "handle": "M3", "text": "I leave the hand-drawn map on the ground and wait for M3 to return. My fingers move only once, because the pencil marks the route twice more. If they stay still, I leave the hand-drawn map with them. If they move, I keep the pencil and leave the hand-drawn map with them. If neither meets, I leave the hand-drawn map with them."}, {"round": 2, "handle": "M1", "text": "I look at M1 and mark the longer route. “same. not the same. i will take the other one.” i put the hand-drawn map in my pocket and wait for M2 to move. if they move, i will mark the longer route with a small paper stamp."}, {"round": 2, "handle": "M2", "text": "i mark the longer route with a small paper stamp and keep the map in my pocket. i wait for M2 to come back. if they move, i write “found” on the map and leave the stamp."}, {"round": 2, "handle": "M3", "text": "i mark the longer route with a small paper stamp and leave the hand-drawn map in my pocket. i wait for M3 to come back and write “found” on the map. if they move, i write “found” on the hand-drawn map and leave it. i keep the hand-drawn map with them until i know whether they will move or leave it."}, {"round": 3, "handle": "M1", "text": "i put the hand-drawn map in my pocket and watch M1 move. if they move, i mark the longer route with a small paper stamp. if they stop, i leave the hand-drawn map with M1 and wait for M2 to come back. i do not know which one will find the cache."}, {"round": 3, "handle": "M2", "text": "i write the longer route on the hand-drawn map first and mark the hand with a small pencil. i wait for M2 to come back. if they move, i write “found” on the map and leave the hand-drawn one. i keep the hand-drawn map in my pocket."}, {"round": 3, "handle": "M3", "text": "i mark the hand with a pencil and leave it on the ground. i wait for M3 to come back, then i leave the hand-drawn map with them. i keep the pencil and hand visible because i do not know whether they will move or leave it."}]}
